// Title: DNS-over-HTTPS Enabled by Registry
// Sigma ID: 04b45a8a-d11d-49e4-9acc-4a1b524407a5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Austin Songer
// Date: 2021-07-22 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, stealth, defense-impairment, T1140, T1112
// Description: Detects when a user enables DNS-over-HTTPS. This can be used to hide internet activity or be
//   used to hide the process of exfiltrating data. With this enabled organization will lose
//   visibility into data such as query type, response and originating IP that are used to determine
//   bad actors.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.tenforums.com/tutorials/151318-how-enable-disable-dns-over-https-doh-microsoft-edge.html
//   - https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/issues/1371
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/?policy=DnsOverHttpsMode
//   - https://admx.help/HKLM/Software/Policies/Mozilla/Firefox/DNSOverHTTPS
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dns_over_https_enabled.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\BuiltInDnsClientEnabled" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)") or (RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Google\\Chrome\\DnsOverHttpsMode" and RegistryValueData =~ "secure") or (RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNSOverHTTPS\\Enabled" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)")
